      "eyebrow": "CCTV and the law",
      "heading": "Signs, retention and UK GDPR",
      "html": "<p>Under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018, the operator needs a lawful reason, clear signs, and a retention period. The ICO publishes video surveillance guidance. In England and Wales the Surveillance Camera Code of Practice adds principles for public space.</p><p>On your walk, check: is the sign there and readable? Is footage kept for the stated time, and no longer? Quickler keeps the sign photo and the retention setting. Whether the use is lawful is for your data protection officer. Check the latest ICO guidance.</p>"
