      "heading": "Doors, readers and failure",
      "html": "<p>Test that a valid credential opens the door and an invalid one does not. Then check what happens when power fails. An escape-route door usually must fail safe. A secure-area door may fail secure. A wrong choice is a fire safety problem too.</p><p>Quickler records each door, its test and its fail state, with a photo. It does not sign off the design. The installer and the responsible person do.</p>"
